# Component Usage

Always check for and use existing components from `/app/components/` before writing custom HTML. Only skip using components if explicitly told not to use them.

## Component Usage Syntax

Use `{% component %}` tags with appropriate parameters:

```html
{% component "button"
    text="Create"
    classes="btn-primary"
    icon="fa-solid fa-plus"
    extra_kwargs={
        "hx-get": "{% url 'myapp:create' %}",
        "hx_modal_toggle": True,
    }
%}
```

For components with slots, prefer using default slots (without `{% slot %}` tag) when possible - it's cleaner to read:

```html
{% component "card" title="Settings" icon="fa-solid fa-gear" %}
    <!-- Content goes directly into default slot -->
    <p>Card content here</p>
{% endcomponent %}
```

Only use explicit `{% slot %}` tags when you need to target a specific named slot (not the default):

```html
{% component "card" title="Settings" icon="fa-solid fa-gear" %}
    {% slot body %}
        <!-- Explicit slot usage - only when needed -->
        <p>Card content here</p>
    {% endslot %}
{% endcomponent %}
```

## Checking Components

Before writing custom HTML:

1. Check `/app/components/` directory for existing components
2. Review component Python files (e.g., `button.py`) to understand available parameters
3. Look at component templates for usage examples
4. Check existing template files for component usage patterns

## Exception

Only skip using components if the user explicitly requests not to use them or if no suitable component exists for the specific use case.
